# The base stage copies requirements.txt alone; the builder stage copies the
# whole repo. So this file is no longer "deny everything" — it is the list of
# things that must not reach the build context, either because they would
# invalidate the layer cache on every commit or because they have no business
# inside an image.
#
# Two entries are load-bearing rather than tidy:
#
#   .env      real credentials. `COPY . src/syncai_backend` would bake them into
#             the image, and main.py's load_dotenv() would then read them in
#             preference to nothing, quietly ignoring compose's environment.
#   .git      several MB that change on every commit, for no build input.
#
# Note what is NOT here: `.interface/`, the optional FAST-LIO2 interface package
# the builder picks up (see the Dockerfile header). It has to reach the context
# to be built.

.git
.github
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# Python / colcon / tooling artefacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
build/
install/
log/

# Secrets and local settings
.env
.claude/settings.local.json

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
